{
  "_comment": "Canonical, single source of truth for the vehicle signal catalog. Both the firmware (via tools/gen_catalog.py -> core/vehicle/src/signal_catalog.generated.inc) and the Mac monitor tool (tools/monitor) read this file. Byte fields are UDS read-data-by-identifier (service 0x22) DID pairs. A signal's displayed value is transform(over each request's (raw + offset) * scale). 'transform' names a C++ function (transform_<name>) defined in signal_catalog.cpp AND a Python function in tools/monitor; 'default' returns request 0's value. Edit here, then run tools/gen_catalog.py. CADENCE FLOOR: no signal polls faster than 50ms. The five signals below that were previously at 20ms -- Int Pres (4), Engine Speed (7), Engine Torque (8), Throttle Pos (12), Int Pres Act. (22) -- were raised to 50ms on 2026-08-25 to match INFO_SCREEN_REFRESH_MS (src/main.cpp), since the display restates values at 20Hz. 'cycle_time_ms' is a FLOOR, not a fixed period: core::SignalPoller polls only the signals currently on a panel, one request outstanding at a time, so a signal is asked for no faster than this and slower whenever the ECU cannot serve full demand. Lowering these back to 20 would not put 20ms of traffic on the bus -- it would only raise their share of whatever throughput the ECU gives. See core/vehicle/README.md.",
  "unit_types": [
    "None",
    "Degrees",
    "Percent",
    "Pressure",
    "RPM",
    "Speed",
    "Temp",
    "Torque",
    "Volume"
  ],
